1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,451
Today is September 24, 2026.

3
00:00:07,451 --> 00:00:13,996
Overnight, the S and P five hundred shed fifty-nine points, down three quarters of one percent.

4
00:00:13,996 --> 00:00:19,375
The Nasdaq dropped over three hundred points, stalling just below its prior high.

5
00:00:19,375 --> 00:00:22,219
The Dow followed lower in sympathy.

6
00:00:22,219 --> 00:00:26,091
The five-year Treasury yield broke above five percent.

7
00:00:26,091 --> 00:00:29,535
That is the highest reading since 2023.

8
00:00:29,535 --> 00:00:32,427
The two-year sits at four point nine.

9
00:00:32,427 --> 00:00:36,373
The thirty-year mortgage has climbed to seven point one two.

10
00:00:36,373 --> 00:00:39,510
The Fed path is the core pressure right now.

11
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:44,326
CME futures price a sixty-nine percent chance of an October hike.

12
00:00:44,326 --> 00:00:47,353
A December follow-up is nearly locked in.

13
00:00:47,353 --> 00:00:50,454
Three hikes this year is the base case.

14
00:00:50,454 --> 00:00:55,074
The S and P Global Services PMI hit fifty-eight point four.

15
00:00:55,074 --> 00:00:58,591
That is the strongest reading since 2021.

16
00:00:58,591 --> 00:01:03,003
Strong services data keeps the Fed firmly on a hawkish footing.

17
00:01:03,003 --> 00:01:06,704
The prior market thesis was that rate cuts were limited.

18
00:01:06,704 --> 00:01:09,008
That assumption is cracking.

19
00:01:09,008 --> 00:01:11,814
Higher-for-longer is back on the table.

20
00:01:11,814 --> 00:01:14,804
Geopolitics added fuel overnight.

21
00:01:14,804 --> 00:01:17,439
US-Iran talks collapsed.

22
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:20,993
Tehran refused to reopen the Strait of Hormuz.

23
00:01:20,993 --> 00:01:25,675
Super tanker rates spiked past one point two million dollars per day.

24
00:01:25,675 --> 00:01:31,103
JPMorgan warns traditional supply-demand models no longer anchor oil pricing.

25
00:01:31,103 --> 00:01:36,765
Bank of America models a one-hundred-fifty-dollar Brent in a prolonged disruption scenario.

26
00:01:36,765 --> 00:01:39,621
A more structural shift is underway.

27
00:01:39,621 --> 00:01:44,670
For the first time, analysts are cutting earnings forecasts faster than raising them.

28
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:51,569
Energy costs, higher borrowing, and sticky services inflation are squeezing margins from both sides.

29
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:56,655
Citi data shows global short positions building across asset classes.

30
00:01:56,655 --> 00:02:00,871
The risk-off tide is spreading from Europe into US equities.

31
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:05,724
In Europe, HSBC downgraded French sovereign debt to underweight.

32
00:02:05,724 --> 00:02:09,351
The euro slid to a two-month low against the dollar.

33
00:02:09,351 --> 00:02:11,949
German two-year yields jumped.

34
00:02:11,949 --> 00:02:15,050
The DAX saw fresh short accumulation.

35
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:19,988
Now the macro liquidity picture is directly repricing the tech complex.

36
00:02:19,988 --> 00:02:23,665
Higher rates hit long-duration growth stocks hardest.

37
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:27,402
That is the Nasdaq's structural vulnerability right now.

38
00:02:27,402 --> 00:02:30,858
But the AI capex cycle is not pausing.

39
00:02:30,858 --> 00:02:37,170
Over two-thirds of enterprises have pushed AI budgets above ten percent of total IT spend.

40
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:41,079
Compute demand is accelerating, not decelerating.

41
00:02:41,079 --> 00:02:44,130
The model price war is intensifying.

42
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:49,878
OpenAI launched GPT six Soul at two dollars per million input tokens.

43
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:55,074
GPT six Luna sits at ten cents input, fifty cents output.

44
00:02:55,074 --> 00:02:59,069
Anthropic countered with Claude Opus five point five.

45
00:02:59,069 --> 00:03:02,513
Input at four dollars, output at twenty.

46
00:03:02,513 --> 00:03:06,214
That is a twenty percent cut from the prior generation.

47
00:03:06,214 --> 00:03:09,657
The old slow-down-iteration consensus is dead.

48
00:03:09,657 --> 00:03:13,628
Inference cost and deployment scale are the new battleground.

49
00:03:13,628 --> 00:03:19,302
On the hardware side, server CPUs and memory are the clear beneficiaries.

50
00:03:19,302 --> 00:03:25,000
AMD and Intel server chip logic is being re-priced by institutional flows.

51
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:31,287
McKinsey data shows a thirty-fold gap in compute consumption across different AI agent workloads.

52
00:03:31,287 --> 00:03:35,466
That gap is driving hardware differentiation at the top end.

53
00:03:35,466 --> 00:03:42,537
The critical divergence from here: companies owning silicon, memory, and manufacturing capacity keep winning.

54
00:03:42,537 --> 00:03:47,758
Pure application-layer firms face price compression and unproven monetization.

55
00:03:47,758 --> 00:03:50,736
AI is no longer a blanket bid.

56
00:03:50,736 --> 00:03:54,375
Trump's July trade disclosures add a data point.

57
00:03:54,375 --> 00:03:58,224
He sold Microsoft, Amazon, and Oracle.

58
00:03:58,224 --> 00:04:03,750
He bought Marvell, Intuit, Salesforce, Adobe, and CrowdStrike.

59
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:06,741
The cloud mega-cap exit is notable.

60
00:04:06,741 --> 00:04:09,167
Let me go into three names.

61
00:04:09,167 --> 00:04:12,415
Meta is the day's most contested narrative.

62
00:04:12,415 --> 00:04:16,165
The stock broke out of a months-long downtrend this week.

63
00:04:16,165 --> 00:04:19,216
A new all-time high is within reach.

64
00:04:19,216 --> 00:04:24,608
The catalyst is Muse, its AI agent platform, unveiled at Connect.

65
00:04:24,608 --> 00:04:28,322
Zuckerberg fronted the two-day livestream personally.

66
00:04:28,322 --> 00:04:34,192
JPMorgan sees Meta as the broadest consumer AI platform after ChatGPT.

67
00:04:34,192 --> 00:04:37,304
Their target is eight hundred twenty dollars.

68
00:04:37,304 --> 00:04:39,645
They maintain an overweight.

69
00:04:39,645 --> 00:04:43,162
But the short side has three structural arguments.

70
00:04:43,162 --> 00:04:46,532
First, Amazon banned Muse outright.

71
00:04:46,532 --> 00:04:51,324
Six major banks issued joint fraud warnings on agent-driven payments.

72
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:55,324
Second, a critical security flaw was disclosed.

73
00:04:55,274 --> 00:05:00,470
Attackers could remotely hijack Muse and harvest multi-platform credentials.

74
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:03,975
Meta patched it, but the trust damage lingers.

75
00:05:03,975 --> 00:05:09,024
Third, the AI phone-call feature still relies on human operators.

76
00:05:09,024 --> 00:05:13,558
When merchants detect the bot, calls transfer to outsourced staff.

77
00:05:13,558 --> 00:05:16,867
At scale, that cost model breaks.

78
00:05:16,867 --> 00:05:20,237
The deeper problem is the business model itself.

79
00:05:20,237 --> 00:05:25,249
An agent that helps users compare and buy faster kills the ad-duration model.

80
00:05:25,249 --> 00:05:28,240
It also kills the search-traffic model.

81
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:32,137
Neither revenue engine maps cleanly to agent commerce.

82
00:05:32,137 --> 00:05:35,678
Subscription conversion ceilings remain unproven.

83
00:05:35,678 --> 00:05:39,980
Revenue contribution against Meta's capex bill is still thin.

84
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:44,391
The entry-point thesis has a structural gap that has not been closed.

85
00:05:44,391 --> 00:05:47,896
McDonald's dropped nearly five percent yesterday.

86
00:05:47,896 --> 00:05:52,406
The stock has fallen from three hundred thirty-four to two hundred thirty-eight.

87
00:05:52,406 --> 00:05:56,646
That is a thirty percent drawdown on a historically low-beta name.

88
00:05:56,646 --> 00:06:01,585
The CEO's own words make this a persistent headwind, not a one-off.

89
00:06:01,585 --> 00:06:07,210
High inflation, weak foot traffic, and rising beef and labor costs will linger.

90
00:06:07,210 --> 00:06:09,710
The strategy shift is telling.

91
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:11,916
No new growth cake.

92
00:06:11,916 --> 00:06:16,034
The play is stealing share through discounts and surgical pricing.

93
00:06:16,034 --> 00:06:18,852
That is a margin-compression playbook.

94
00:06:18,852 --> 00:06:23,534
They plan to deploy eight point five billion dollars to franchisees.

95
00:06:23,534 --> 00:06:28,460
Restaurant modernization, tech deployment, operational upgrades.

96
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:33,803
Target is ten thousand dollars in added annual cash flow per US location.

97
00:06:33,803 --> 00:06:38,583
The fifty percent operating margin target by 2030 is ambitious.

98
00:06:38,583 --> 00:06:42,369
But the path there runs through a prolonged cost squeeze.

99
00:06:42,369 --> 00:06:47,247
At three percent dividend yield, the valuation floor has some support.

100
00:06:47,247 --> 00:06:52,308
But the fundamental trajectory argues for a slow bleed, not a V-recovery.

101
00:06:52,308 --> 00:06:54,624
Patience over panic here.

102
00:06:54,624 --> 00:06:58,350
Marvell is the quiet semiconductor winner in this tape.

103
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:01,475
Trump's July buy list includes the name.

104
00:07:01,475 --> 00:07:05,494
The stock sits under two hundred thirty billion in market cap.

105
00:07:05,494 --> 00:07:10,556
The setup is optical interconnect and custom silicon for AI data centers.

106
00:07:10,556 --> 00:07:15,458
Jensen Huang has referenced a trillion-dollar addressable market for this space.

107
00:07:15,458 --> 00:07:17,553
The chart is intact.

108
00:07:17,553 --> 00:07:19,894
Uptrend structure holds.

109
00:07:19,894 --> 00:07:22,308
No major support break.

110
00:07:22,308 --> 00:07:25,801
The name is in accumulation, not distribution.

111
00:07:25,801 --> 00:07:28,362
The risk is the rate environment.

112
00:07:28,362 --> 00:07:33,987
If the Fed hikes three times, long-duration growth multiples compress across the board.

113
00:07:33,987 --> 00:07:36,168
Marvell is not immune.

114
00:07:36,168 --> 00:07:39,588
But the capex cycle supports the revenue line.

115
00:07:39,588 --> 00:07:43,963
As long as hyperscalers build, Marvell's order book holds.

116
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:48,313
Watch the next earnings print for data-center revenue acceleration.

117
00:07:48,313 --> 00:07:51,744
Support sits at the fifty-day moving average.

118
00:07:51,744 --> 00:07:55,568
A close below that invalidates the short-term structure.

119
00:07:55,568 --> 00:07:58,423
Resistance is the prior swing high.

120
00:07:58,423 --> 00:08:02,431
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

121
00:08:02,431 --> 00:08:06,597
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
